From cdc2d4940f401ee6ad5588810a70f35a9df47328 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:10:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pdlc: add steps.py for the fixed sequences of a stage

A new script, pdlc/bin/steps.py, does the fixed sequences that the acceptance, tests, and
`verify` skills make by hand. It has three subcommands.

- lock (IN-xxxx or CH-xxxx) makes the commit of the checks, writes the lock hash, makes
  the lock commit, and makes the tests packet. It also runs the writing check on the text
  of the two commits, because the commit hook does not see the commits of a script.
- checks (CH-xxxx) runs each item that `verify` needs. It prints one line for each item,
  and the pass commit.
- verified (CH-xxxx) sets the statuses of a passed round, and makes the commit
  "Verified CH-xxxx".

The script reuses the functions of check_merge.py, make_packets.py and record_merges.py.
Each refusal prints one line and commits nothing.

The README gets the form of the acceptance lines of config.md, and a bullet about lock.
The acceptance skill points to that form. The `verify` skill names the checks and verified
subcommands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
